WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.663
Hi, I'm Thole!

00:00:02.663 --> 00:00:05.522
This video model writes a clip chunk by chunk.

00:00:05.522 --> 00:00:08.381
One extra training loss teaches it what happens next.

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:13.664
The idea: from the current chunk alone, side predictors must draw chunks

00:00:13.664 --> 00:00:16.462
further ahead, with the gap hidden and no prompt.

00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:23.393
Usually the model sees the real history and denoises the next chunk.

00:00:23.393 --> 00:00:27.032
Neighbouring chunks look alike, so continuing the past almost works.

00:00:27.452 --> 00:00:31.529
Ask for a chunk further out, with the gap hidden, and continuity stops helping.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.549
The generator reads the clean history and the current chunk, and

00:00:36.549 --> 00:00:37.791
builds its hidden states.

00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:41.419
Those feed side predictors, one per offset, each with its own

00:00:41.419 --> 00:00:42.585
weights and no prompt.

00:00:43.005 --> 00:00:46.582
Each predictor denoises a chunk further ahead, and its loss flows

00:00:46.582 --> 00:00:47.882
back into the generator.

00:00:48.302 --> 00:00:50.818
At inference, every predictor is deleted.

00:00:50.818 --> 00:00:53.334
The generator runs exactly as before.

00:00:54.608 --> 00:00:57.490
Chain the heads, and each inherits a noisy copy of the chunk

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.451
it should not see.

00:00:59.615 --> 00:01:03.761
In parallel, the only route to the future runs through the current chunk's features.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:11.429
Sampled from the current chunk alone, the next-chunk predictor tracks the real wave closely.

00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:14.910
Three chunks out, detail goes, but the curl and break remain.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:20.170
On the five billion model, the score rises from thirty point four

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:21.515
to thirty-three point eight.

00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:23.197
Chained heads reach only thirty-one.

00:01:24.508 --> 00:01:28.187
They are not small: about three and a half billion extra parameters,

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:29.413
though only during training.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:35.530
Make the current chunk's features predict a later chunk, with the gap

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:38.249
hidden, and the gains show up in when things move.

00:01:41.358 --> 00:01:45.142
To recap: predict ahead from the current chunk, keep the heads parallel,

00:01:45.142 --> 00:01:46.719
and drop them before inference.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.213
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.213 --> 00:01:49.806
I'm Thole.

00:01:49.806 --> 00:01:50.102
Bye!
